FaceIdentify schema migrations (PERSISTENCE_IMPLEMENTATION.md §27).

Alembic is the only way the production schema is created or changed: never call
`Base.metadata.create_all()` outside a test that is comparing against it.

The library database's path comes from the FACEIDENTIFY_DATABASE_PATH environment variable
(no Storage Manager exists yet to resolve it). Run from the repository root:

    $env:FACEIDENTIFY_DATABASE_PATH = "C:\path\to\library.db"
    uv run alembic upgrade head                 # create/upgrade the schema
    uv run alembic upgrade head --sql           # print the SQL instead (no database needed)
    uv run alembic downgrade base               # drop every table (development only)
    uv run alembic check                        # fail if the models drifted from the migrations

Changing a model means adding a reviewed revision:

    uv run alembic revision --autogenerate --rev-id 0002 -m "short description"

Then read the generated file: autogenerate does not detect CHECK-constraint changes, and it does
not know about data. SQLite can only change most constraints by recreating the table, so use
`op.batch_alter_table` (batch mode is already on in env.py). tests/integration/test_migrations.py
fails if the models and the migrations disagree.
